1
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:08,680
Six friends share a pizza bill.

2
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:13,290
The bill is 38 dollars 70, and they split it equally.

3
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:15,340
How much does each friend pay?

4
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:18,920
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:21,080
We need 38.70 divided by 6.

6
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:27,490
Estimate first: 36 divided by 6 is 6, so the answer is a bit more than 6.

7
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:29,520
The exact answer is 6.45.

8
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:31,960
Each friend pays 6 dollars 45.

9
00:00:32,010 --> 00:00:35,030
Let's see how to work that out.

10
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,190
Remember short division.

11
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,270
774 divided by 6.

12
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:42,270
7 divided by 6 is 1, remainder 1.

13
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:44,910
Carry the 1 to make 17.

14
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:48,230
17 divided by 6 is 2, remainder 5.

15
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:50,480
Carry the 5 to make 54.

16
00:00:50,530 --> 00:00:52,530
54 divided by 6 is 9.

17
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:54,830
The answer is 129.

18
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:58,740
To divide a decimal by a whole number, use short division.

19
00:00:58,790 --> 00:01:04,610
Write the decimal point in the answer directly above the point in the question.

20
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:06,420
38.70 divided by 6.

21
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:09,760
3 divided by 6 is 0, so look at 38.

22
00:01:09,810 --> 00:01:13,550
38 divided by 6 is 6, remainder 2.

23
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:18,070
Now we reach the decimal point, so put a point in the answer.

24
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,210
Carry the 2 to make 27.

25
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:23,390
27 divided by 6 is 4, remainder 3.

26
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:26,360
Then 30 divided by 6 is 5.

27
00:01:26,410 --> 00:01:28,960
The answer is 6.45.

28
00:01:29,010 --> 00:01:29,730
Your turn.

29
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:31,720
Work out 8.4 divided by 2.

30
00:01:31,770 --> 00:01:35,190
Pause the video and try it.

31
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:36,920
8 divided by 2 is 4.

32
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:38,300
Write the point.

33
00:01:38,350 --> 00:01:40,030
4 divided by 2 is 2.

34
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:42,130
The answer is 4.2.

35
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:45,030
Sometimes there is a remainder at the end.

36
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:50,130
Then write extra zeros after the decimal point, and keep dividing.

37
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,320
7.3 divided by 4.

38
00:01:52,370 --> 00:01:55,320
Write 7.3 as 7.300.

39
00:01:55,370 --> 00:01:58,440
7 divided by 4 is 1, remainder 3.

40
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:01,660
33 divided by 4 is 8, remainder 1.

41
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:04,870
10 divided by 4 is 2, remainder 2.

42
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:07,410
20 divided by 4 is 5.

43
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:10,150
The answer is 1.825.

44
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:11,550
Here is the method.

45
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,790
Step 1: estimate first.

46
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,970
Step 2: set out short division.

47
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:20,900
Write the point in the answer above the point in the question.

48
00:02:20,950 --> 00:02:25,380
Step 3: divide digit by digit, carrying the remainders.

49
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:30,010
Step 4: if there is a remainder at the end, add zeros and carry on.

50
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:32,360
Then check by multiplying.

51
00:02:32,410 --> 00:02:35,050
Work out 14.56 divided by 4.

52
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:38,580
Estimate: 16 divided by 4 is 4.

53
00:02:38,630 --> 00:02:41,530
14 divided by 4 is 3, remainder 2.

54
00:02:41,580 --> 00:02:44,150
Write 3, then the point.

55
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:47,470
25 divided by 4 is 6, remainder 1.

56
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,060
16 divided by 4 is 4.

57
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:51,620
The answer is 3.64.

58
00:02:51,670 --> 00:02:55,020
That is close to the estimate of 4.

59
00:02:55,070 --> 00:02:55,740
Your turn.

60
00:02:55,790 --> 00:02:57,470
Work out 3 divided by 8.

61
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:59,410
You will need to add zeros.

62
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:02,390
Pause and work it out.

63
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:04,160
Write 3 as 3.000.

64
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:07,700
30 divided by 8 is 3, remainder 6.

65
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:11,240
60 divided by 8 is 7, remainder 4.

66
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:13,430
40 divided by 8 is 5.

67
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:16,070
The answer is 0.375.

68
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:18,880
Work out 52.8 divided by 16.

69
00:03:18,930 --> 00:03:22,640
Estimate: 48 divided by 16 is 3.

70
00:03:22,690 --> 00:03:28,470
It helps to list the multiples of 16: 16, 32, 48, 64.

71
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:31,760
52 divided by 16 is 3, remainder 4.

72
00:03:31,810 --> 00:03:33,260
Write the point.

73
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:35,790
Then 48 divided by 16 is 3.

74
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,020
The answer is 3.3.

75
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:40,150
A plank is 2.85 metres long.

76
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:42,420
It is cut into 5 equal pieces.

77
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:45,930
How long is each piece, in centimetres?

78
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:50,090
2.85 divided by 5 is 0.57 metres.

79
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:54,070
Multiply by 100 to change metres to centimetres.

80
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:57,430
Each piece is 57 centimetres long.

81
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,880
Max works out 7.2 divided by 3.

82
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:02,010
Which line is wrong?

83
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:03,110
Line 3 is wrong.

84
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,100
Max forgot the decimal point.

85
00:04:05,150 --> 00:04:09,420
It goes in the answer, straight above the point in 7.2.

86
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:10,850
The answer is 2.4.

87
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:16,720
An estimate helps: 7 divided by 3 is about 2, so 24 is far too big.

88
00:04:16,770 --> 00:04:21,960
A marathon is a very exact distance: 42.195 kilometres.

89
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:25,830
A half marathon is that distance divided by 2.

90
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:31,710
42 divided by 2 is 21, and 0.195 divided by 2 is 0.0975.

91
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:35,710
A half marathon is 21.0975 kilometres.

92
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:39,410
That is about 21.1 kilometres.

93
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:40,790
One last question.

94
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,710
What is 0.9 divided by 3?

95
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:46,180
Pause the video and answer.

96
00:04:46,230 --> 00:04:49,040
9 tenths divided by 3 is 3 tenths.

97
00:04:49,090 --> 00:04:51,110
The answer is 0.3.

98
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:56,650
To remember: put the point in the answer, above the point in the question.

99
00:04:56,700 --> 00:05:00,260
Divide digit by digit, carrying remainders.

100
00:05:00,310 --> 00:05:03,680
Add zeros after the point to keep dividing.

101
00:05:03,730 --> 00:05:07,090
Estimate first, and check by multiplying.

102
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:12,190
Great work! Now practise lesson 4.4 on Camday.
